      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-c26a34bb-1cfd-48ec-8205-e6c43c88a41a-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 5px; border: none;">
<h2 style="text-align: center; line-height: 1.2; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 18px;" align="center">City of Columbus Pre-kindergarten Initiative</h2>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Mayor Andrew J. Ginther’s vision for America’s Opportunity City is universal access to a high-quality pre-kindergarten education for every 4-year-old in Columbus.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Established by the city in 2014, Early Start Columbus (ESC) awards grants to community-based providers to help increase the number of children who enter kindergarten ready to learn.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">If your center is located within Franklin County, is in good standing with all licensing bodies and has achieved either a silver or gold rating in Step Up To Quality, Ohio’s Tiered Quality Rating and Improvement System, <strong>we invite you to submit a letter of intent to apply for funding for the 2025-2026 school year</strong>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Children served must be four years old by September 30, 2025 and reside within the boundaries of Franklin County. Pre-kindergarten services must be offered for a full day (five hours of instruction per day, exclusive of before and after care, recesses and breakfast/lunch periods) and for the school year (approximately 850 hours). The family income of children served must be no more than 300% of the Federal Poverty Level (FPL).</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">To submit your Letter of Intent, log into e-CImpact (if new, create an account using your agency EIN) via this link <a href="https://agency.e-cimpact.com/login.aspx?org=37145F&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">https://agency.e-cimpact.com/login.aspx?org=37145F</a>.  Once logged in, go to Grant Applications and select the Pre-Kindergarten Initiative Letter of Intent 2025. For questions or assistance navigating the e-CImpact system, please email <a href="mailto:reporting.help@uwcentralohio.org" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">reporting.help@uwcentralohio.org</a>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Please submit your letter of intent to apply, indicating how your organization meets these preliminary requirements, by April 4, 2025</strong>. Application materials for the 2025-2026 school year will be sent to you upon receipt of your letter of intent to apply.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">We look forward to partnering with you to help expand pre-kindergarten opportunities for our Columbus children. If you have any questions, please feel free to email us at <a href="mailto:education@columbus.gov" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">education@columbus.gov</a>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"> </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Sincerely,</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Mayor's Office of Education</p>
